 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [NeRF Training Configuration](1203-nerf-training-configuration.md)
-Defines the optimization loop, data handling, and regularization strategies. It focuses on the standard MLP architecture and training dynamics, distinguishing itself from variants like [NeRF-SH](1348-nerf-sh.md) which modify the output representation.
+Defines the optimization loop, data handling, and regularization strategies required to train a NeRF model, distinguishing itself by focusing on standard MLP dynamics rather than explicit surface constraints.
 
 ### [NeRF-SH](1348-nerf-sh.md)
-Replaces direct RGB output with spherical harmonic coefficients, enabling efficient storage in octrees and real-time rendering. It differs from the original NeRF by eliminating viewing direction as a network input for color.
+Replaces direct RGB output with spherical harmonic coefficients to eliminate viewing direction as a network input, enabling efficient storage in octrees and faster rendering.
 
 ### [Recursive-NeRF](3029-recursive-nerf.md)
-Uses a hierarchy of branch networks based on uncertainty, allowing dynamic network depth. It differs from standard NeRF by early-terminating simple regions to reduce computation.
+Routes query points through a hierarchy of branch networks based on uncertainty, reducing computational load in simple regions.
 
 ### [Mip-NeRF](3381-mip-nerf.md)
-Renders anti-aliased conical frustums instead of rays to handle multi-scale details. It differs from standard NeRF by integrating positional encoding over the volume of the frustum.
+Renders anti-aliased conical frustums instead of infinitesimal rays to reduce aliasing artifacts.
 
 ### [NeMF (Neural Microflake Field)](3387-nemf-neural-microflake-field.md)
-Models light transportation via microflake normals and roughness. It differs from standard NeRF by explicitly modeling physical attributes rather than just radiance.
+Models light transportation via microflake normals and roughness to handle complex geometry and translucency.
 
 ### [EgoNeRF](4096-egonerf.md)
-Uses a spherical feature grid for large-scale egocentric scenes. It differs from standard NeRF by using a spherical coordinate system to match capture geometry.
+Adapts NeRF for large-scale egocentric scenes using a spherical feature grid.
 
 ### [Intrinsic NeRF](4623-intrinsic-nerf.md)
-Decouples geometry, illumination, and material. It differs from standard NeRF by outputting separate shading and reflectance components.
+Decouples geometry, illumination, and material properties for relighting tasks.
 
 ### [Sparse Neural Volume Representation](7055-sparse-neural-volume-representation.md)
-Uses a sparse 3D grid of per-voxel features. It differs from standard NeRF by using explicit voxel features for memory efficiency.
+Uses a sparse 3D grid of per-voxel neural features for scalability.
 
 ### [Instant Neural Graphics Primitives (Instant NGP)](8637-instant-neural-graphics-primitives-instant-ngp.md)
-Replaces the MLP with a Multi-resolution Hash Encoding. It differs from standard NeRF by drastically reducing training time and enabling real-time rendering.
+Accelerates NeRF using multi-resolution hash encoding to reduce training time to minutes.
